2025-05-01 03:03:25 - Thread-1158 (execute) - INFO - [Exploration]
Relevant columns and their possible usage  
• `event_name` : filter to sessions (`'session_start'`).  
• `event_date` : string `YYYYMMDD`; used to ① get the user’s first contact date, ② put every event into the correct calendar week, and ③ calculate the distance in weeks between two contacts.  
• `user_pseudo_id` : anonymous GA4 identifier of a visitor; required to join all the events that belong to the same user.  
• `event_timestamp` : could be used when two events for the same user fall on the same calendar‑day and we need the very first one, but the task only requires the first **day**, so the column is optional.  

Typical conditions  
• `event_name = 'session_start'` – keep only session starts.  
• `event_date >= '20180702'` – ignore everything before the first Monday we care about.  
• `DATE_TRUNC(PARSE_DATE('%Y%m%d',event_date), WEEK(MONDAY))  AS cohort_week` – build Monday based cohorts.  
• `weeks_since_cohort = FLOOR(DATE_DIFF(PARSE_DATE('%Y%m%d',event_date), cohort_week, DAY)/7)` – distance to the cohort week; keep `weeks_since_cohort = 3` for 4‑week retention.  

